WEBVTT

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.810
Run at once towards a dream

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.810
yume no mukou e ikkini hashitte yo

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.780
Let’s meet and laugh away yesterday’s troubles

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.780
nayameru kinou wo fungiri warai aou

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.860
When our memories were here,

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.860
omoide ga itta no toki mo

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.060
even though we are deeply hurt, go straight on

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.060
kizu wo fukai no ni massugu mae ni

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.650
GO TO NEW WORLD

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:54.470
I can feel it in the wind

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:54.470
kaze no naka kanjiteru yo

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:58.130
The hot beat is shining

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:58.130
atsui kodou kagayaku yo

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:00.610
especially now…

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:00.610
ima koso

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.550
surely, always, you’ll be by my side

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.550
kitto zutto soba ni iru yo ne

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:12.410
Keep on running the way to the future.

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:12.410
mirai no michi wo hashiri tsuzukeyou

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:17.300
more and more, no matter what happens

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:17.300
motto motto nani ga okitemo

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:21.510
half our tears become double smiles

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:21.510
namida wa hanbun nibai no egao ni naru

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.060
forever

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:24.060
itsudemo

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.590
We would like to request jobs from you.

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:53.480
Huh?

00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:56.380
Two years ago…

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.610
There was a pair of crying twins that I tightly embraced.

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:18.070
Don’t cry… okay?

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:23.080
The night came soon,
as well as the morning…

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.480
And then, the next evening came again.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.650
So many things have changed in the last two years.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:30.330
Like this situation in bed.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.780
The two junior high students I embraced at the riverbed two years ago…

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:39.380
are now high school students, sleeping right next to me.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.610
HOW NOISY!!!

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.430
Seems there will be beautiful weather today in Tokyo.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:02.370
While I am in the office, I am a guardian.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:06.610
Because of that, I, Futaba Rentarou,

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:09.620
have never laid a hand on the
high school students in question.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:14.530
That is also why, during these two years, I’ve tried not to harbor even one guilty thought.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.840
Even so, nothing could be done about that one phrase…

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.970
You won’t do anything like having illicit sexual relationships, right?

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:28.930
Well…

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:31.330
These “illicit sexual relationships” that you speak of…

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:33.780
It’s unhealthy conduct.

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:36.780
This “conduct” that you speak of…

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:37.680
I’m talking about “pafu-pafu”.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:39.130
This “pafu-pafu” that you speak of…

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:41.030
It’s an illicit sexual relationship.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:47.530
G-Gimme a break! Isn’t it obvious that it will be all right, sensei?

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:49.130
That’s right!

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:50.770
Oh come on, stop already!

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:54.830
See, from an education point of view, they seemed the same.

00:03:57.980 --> 00:03:59.330
Talking about hobbies…

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:00.730
I am perfectly innocent.

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:03.030
That’s good.

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:05.970
That’s right…

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:11.180
Long ago, Rentarou-kun was always fastidious about that sort of thing.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:13.130
No, not to that degree.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:21.880
Umm… Mai-san.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:23.280
I have a job…

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:26.080
that I’d like to ask you to do.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.220
Hey, hey…

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:40.730
Hey, hey, are you angry?

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:43.630
I’m not angry…

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:47.780
Because you were howling all of a sudden, you know…

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:49.080
I got freaked out.

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:51.830
I said that I’m not angry.

00:04:51.830 --> 00:04:55.580
More importantly, what’s up with that getup of yours?

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:59.570
Stakeout-casual or hari-casi! Yay!

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:01.330
Is it weird?

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:03.430
Frankly, it looks like you just popped out of the comics.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:06.530
If we, as usual, dressed the same, our identities would be exposed.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:08.730
The problem isn’t about you being exposed or not.

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:12.530
Bah, how boring!!

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:13.830
Hmph, then go home!

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:15.430
We don’t want to!

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:17.730
This isn’t a game.

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:19.800
Be a little more serious, will ya?

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:23.720
The lunch box has croquettes and omelettes. Which would you like?

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:25.300
AS I SAID…!!!

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.530
Last night, the lady of the Sugisaki meat store gave these croquettes to me you know…

00:05:28.530 --> 00:05:31.310
The name of the client is Momoi Mai.

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:34.950
She works at Futagotamagawa’s private school, Hinashi Senior High,

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:37.030
as the school doctor and counselor.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:40.290
Her request was to investigate around there,

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:43.130
and to report the target’s actions throughout the day.

00:05:43.130 --> 00:05:45.830
It’s unpleasant work, spying on other people’s lives.

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:47.880
The target of the investigation is…

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:48.760
The target is moving!

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:07.230
Ai-san…

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:09.680
Three years ago…

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:12.930
There was a crying pair of twins I tightly embraced.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:17.530
Three years ago, I was in high school,

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:20.630
Mai-san and Ai-san were new teachers.

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:23.980
As it was, it could be said that we got along well.

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:30.880
I can’t do it.

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:33.480
Investigating this person feels like betrayal.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:38.120
Anyway, you and Mai-san are living together,

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.050
and since you’re so close,
if you just asked directly…

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:42.730
She’s off work without permission.

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:45.230
And she wouldn’t call me back on the cell phone.

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:47.330
In the end, she just went out.

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:52.680
She’s been spending a lot of time
at a man’s apartment.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.680
After three years,
many things have changed.

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:02.380
I’m going to follow her.

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:04.980
You both stay here
and watch the apartment.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:08.030
If a man comes out, take a photo without further ado…

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:09.880
and don’t do anything rash.

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:10.980
Rentarou?

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:11.480
What?

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:13.330
Are you acquainted with the target?

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:14.830
N-N-Not at all.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:17.480
Because the way you were gazing at her just then…

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:20.530
E-Even if it was like that,
in doesn’t matter right now.

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:21.430
It doesn’t have anything to do--

00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:23.580
--with us, right?

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:24.680
Yup. Yup.

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:27.380
It really doesn’t concern us, right?

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:28.630
Yup. Yup. Yup.

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:31.380
You can go then!

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:32.720
Right! I’m going!

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:36.680
Like I said! I just wanted to go shopping!

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:40.000
From Shibuya, it seems a stalker-like
individual has been spotted in these parts…

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:41.610
… and has been lurking around.

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:45.200
No, I wasn’t lurking or anything.
I’m a genuine resident of Nikotama.

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:47.980
Well, well, well, I’m feeling bored at the moment.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:50.030
I’ll slowly listen to what you
have to say, okay?

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:51.990
Gimme a break!

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:54.380
Soujyu.

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:55.630
Hmm?

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:58.330
Rentarou lied, right?

00:07:58.330 --> 00:07:59.680
He did.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:01.730
Something’s up with Rentarou, right?

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:03.230
There is.

00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:05.130
Rentarou is so crappy, right?

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:06.170
Oh.

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:10.880
Sara-chan?

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:12.230
Hmm?

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:14.180
Should we investigate?

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:18.380
Should we investigate by ourselves?

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:21.560
Argh, crap!

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:23.080
That damn Hariyama.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:26.380
Wasting time interrogating an honest detective.

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:27.930
Who’s the heavy drinker here?

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:49.080
Sara here!

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:52.230
Sorry, I can’t answer the phone right now.

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:55.350
I will definitely get back to you, so leave a message.

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:56.130
That’s about it.

00:08:58.080 --> 00:08:59.930
It’s me, Rentarou!

00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:01.400
Where are you right now?

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:02.480
Contact me!

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:03.330
That’s all!

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:17.680
Geez, where the heck are they?

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:22.040
Coming!

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:27.880
I’ll be right there. Please hold on a bit, okay?

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:39.350
I came to ask you to do something for me.

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:43.080
Ai-san…

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:02.380
A story about Emerald Mountain.

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:06.380
Oh, it’s sold out?

00:10:06.380 --> 00:10:07.280
It’s fine!

00:10:08.430 --> 00:10:08.790
Ah--

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:14.130
Anything can easily replace the taste of that canned coffee!

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:16.630
Ah! Ai doesn’t understand.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:19.480
The Emerald Mountain is very, very extraordinary…

00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:20.730
Right, Rentarou-kun?

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:24.940
Right! Extraordinary!

00:10:25.110 --> 00:10:26.830
Fine. Fine.

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:30.080
Since I’m a woman who doesn’t understand the taste of coffee, after all.

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:32.610
I’m the wrong friend…

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:35.990
Ah, it was a lie! I’m a great liar!

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:38.120
Lies, lies, lies…
What’s so great about the taste…

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:39.130
Geez…

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:40.750
We’ll do it right away, Ai.

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:43.750
The three of us together:
inseparable friends.

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:46.710
Come on, let the three of us search for the Emerald Mountain!

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:49.780
Agreed!

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:05.380
Umm…

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:06.850
Was there something that you needed from me…

00:11:07.780 --> 00:11:09.780
Ah, silly, silly me.

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:12.580
For Ai-san to come to my house, of course she’d have some sort of business.

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:15.630
Being like a stalker and sneakily coming over isn’t good, eh?

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:18.580
Actually I was caught once doing that. I really was…

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:18.910
Oh?

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:21.130
UWAAH! That’s bad! That’s bad!

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:23.630
Futhermore, where’s such a large amount of coffee supposed to go…

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:25.380
In the first place, this is just ordinary coffee, right?!

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:26.980
I dunno, I dunno, I dunno. It’s too weird.

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:29.630
What the hell is she doing at the Futaba Detective Agency…

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:30.480
Ai-san…?

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:34.180
It seems I dropped my cell phone somewhere.

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:38.760
I was wondering if we could go and search for it together, Futaba-kun.

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:57.380
For now, how about drinking some canned coffee?

00:11:57.980 --> 00:11:59.910
Agreed!

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:04.680
Of course, the brand we typically had was definitely Emerald Mountain.

00:12:06.380 --> 00:12:08.330
Ah, it’s sold out again.

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:09.180
It’s okay!

00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:10.130
Ah--

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:17.730
Since we couldn’t get ahold of Emerald Mountain, it was exactly like back then.

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:20.380
While we were savoring our mocha blend,

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:24.380
we went on a journey to a hundred and fifty places around Nikotama.

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:27.480
Any details about the lost cell phone?

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:28.980
It’s a really old one.

00:12:28.980 --> 00:12:30.380
It hasn’t changed from back then.

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:32.580
Ah, the one that looked like a transceiver.

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:34.230
What era is that from?

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:44.580
Huh? I’ve been down this road before…

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:45.480
This is it.

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:47.630
Once, we were here by car, and everyone got lost.

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:49.580
Ah, I see, I see.

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:50.830
That time with that “Test of Courage”…

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:53.230
Paper, scissors…

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:53.780
There!

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:55.830
Rock! On point!

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:57.430
Ah, I lost again!

00:12:57.430 --> 00:12:59.680
You’re always been weak at rock, paper, scissors.

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:11.630
So, have you remembered where it could be?

00:13:11.630 --> 00:13:15.060
Well, I really can’t remember at all.

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:16.930
Just where did I leave it behind?

00:13:16.930 --> 00:13:18.780
Are you serious?

00:13:18.780 --> 00:13:20.980
But somehow, it’s quite fun.

00:13:20.980 --> 00:13:24.240
Well… It’s not like it wasn’t fun, but…

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:26.380
I’m exhausted.

00:13:26.380 --> 00:13:28.080
Come on, come on, keep going!

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:31.080
You’re a boy, aren’t you?

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:35.130
How many more places are there after this?

00:13:35.130 --> 00:13:38.580
Hmm, there might be a hundred places left, I think.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:40.980
My legs are like lead.

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:43.480
Shall we rest a bit?

00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:44.480
Good idea.

00:13:46.780 --> 00:13:48.530
01:00 PM: She came out of the convenience store.

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:52.080
1:30 PM: There was contact with a man, and she went into Cafe a Latte.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:55.480
2:30 PM: She right-straight punched a man after violently reprimanding him,

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:57.850
followed by a left uppercut, and finished with a brain buster.

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:01.530
3:00 PM: A medic arrived, the man was carried away, and right now he’s gone.

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:03.930
3:30 PM: She ordered something at Cafe a Latte.

00:14:03.930 --> 00:14:04.830
Sara-chan!

00:14:04.830 --> 00:14:06.780
That is a caramel latte.

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.680
She’s drinking caramel latte…

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:10.230
Or a marshmallow latter?

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:12.130
Marshmallow…

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:13.870
Or a Macchiato?

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:16.780
Anything is fine, geez!

00:14:16.780 --> 00:14:18.480
It’s not fine!

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:21.130
Because the taste is totally different!

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:24.180
Gaah, it’s all the same!
Coffee is bitter anyways!

00:14:24.180 --> 00:14:27.780
Sara-chan, you still only drink
apple juice, huh?

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:30.380
You have such childish tastes.

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:32.180
I just don’t drink it ’cause I don’t like it!

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:33.930
Hmph!

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:37.230
You guys…

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:39.560
Aren’t you the assistants from Rentarou-kun’s place?

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:42.490
Well… umm…

00:14:48.930 --> 00:14:50.430
I’m sorry.

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:53.580
These are the same set of clothes as Ai’s.

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:55.830
Not at all. We’re sorry too.

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:57.880
We sure have behaved like little children.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:14:58.880
It’s all right.

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:04.380
Even though you’re twins, your personalities are completely different.

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:06.380
Yes.

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:08.200
Just like us.

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:12.570
Even though we were totally different inside, we got along well.

00:15:13.380 --> 00:15:16.930
The only thing we had in common was a wonderful boy.

00:15:18.380 --> 00:15:21.030
Just about everything was the same.

00:15:37.430 --> 00:15:39.580
We still haven’t found the cell phone.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:40.280
Yeah.

00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:41.580
I’m exhausted.

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:42.330
Yeah.

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.220
Somehow we still haven’t given up on the mission, but…

00:15:44.830 --> 00:15:47.030
how about crying together for a bit of catharsis?

00:15:47.030 --> 00:15:47.760
No thanks.

00:15:51.230 --> 00:15:53.830
Emerald Mountain!!

00:15:57.480 --> 00:16:01.680
Ever since that time, she’s just totally disappeared.

00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:02.880
She’s gone without a trace.

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:04.280
I’ve stopped being a teacher.

00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:06.130
I can’t handle it anymore.

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:08.380
The thing we had held in our hands…

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:12.780
We ended up letting it go.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:18.780
You…

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:22.750
shouldn’t become like us!

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:26.950
By all means, don’t let go of it!

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:30.880
Sister…

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:37.600
Let’s go.

00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:21.560
No! Ai!!

00:17:26.680 --> 00:17:27.430
I know.

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:37.380
Huh?

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:38.580
Ai-san?

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:39.830
Mai-san?

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:43.630
Ai-san!

00:17:43.630 --> 00:17:44.330
Mai-san!

00:17:48.430 --> 00:17:48.980
Ai-san?

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:51.720
Rentarou-kun.

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:57.680
We can’t have it our own way, can we?

00:17:58.030 --> 00:17:58.980
What’s up?

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:00.480
Lots of things.

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:02.780
Lots of things?

00:18:02.780 --> 00:18:06.690
The cell phone, work, the fight with Mai.

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:10.700
And also…

00:18:17.680 --> 00:18:19.140
The classroom at night.

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:23.580
That time… the thing I couldn’t do.

00:18:25.730 --> 00:18:26.580
Ai-san…

00:18:34.730 --> 00:18:38.380
In the end, we weren’t able to find Ai-san’s phone.

00:18:39.580 --> 00:18:41.030
Probably,

00:18:41.030 --> 00:18:44.230
it’s in a far away country,

00:18:44.230 --> 00:18:47.180
sunken in the deep, deep waters of a far away ocean.

00:18:49.080 --> 00:18:50.280
This is Ai.

00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:52.880
I can’t answer the phone right now.

00:18:52.880 --> 00:18:55.430
If you have any concerns, please leave a message.

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:57.730
Rentarou here.

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:00.030
Sorry, I couldn’t find it.

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:02.530
Though, somehow, it was fun.

00:19:03.630 --> 00:19:04.380
Well…

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:08.030
Someday, whenever it’s good,

00:19:08.030 --> 00:19:10.180
if you hear this, please call me then.

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:11.030
I’ll be waiting.

00:19:11.780 --> 00:19:12.630
I’ll be waiting.

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:18.330
Three years have passed, and many things have changed.

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:20.530
Nothing can ever stay the same.

00:19:21.530 --> 00:19:24.030
It’s probably something like that.

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:29.630
The next day, Ai-san vanished from this city.

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:35.200
Shall we go home?

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:37.080
Yes.

00:19:39.130 --> 00:19:39.830
I’m home.

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:47.830
Soujyu?

00:19:48.780 --> 00:19:49.750
Sara!

00:19:50.530 --> 00:19:51.500
Soujyu!

00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:53.010
Sara!

00:19:53.780 --> 00:19:54.780
Heeeey!

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:25.240
I don’t know!

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:29.930
Well…

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:31.980
First off, put in the soup broth…

00:20:31.980 --> 00:20:33.380
After that comes the meat!

00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:34.180
Too fast!

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:35.930
That’s wrong.

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:39.080
First you put the vegetables in
and pour out the water.

00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:41.050
Sara-chan, you’re so forgetful.

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:42.180
Shut up!!

00:20:42.180 --> 00:20:43.970
I don’t know anything about all that!!

00:20:44.380 --> 00:20:46.780
Not knowing that is a sin.

00:20:46.780 --> 00:20:48.190
I’ve been caught.

00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:50.030
HEEEEY!

00:20:50.030 --> 00:20:52.130
It hurts, Sara-chan!

00:20:53.330 --> 00:20:55.230
Ah, it’s Rentarou!

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:56.630
How fast, how fast!

00:20:57.980 --> 00:20:59.930
Today, you know, after lots of effort,

00:20:59.930 --> 00:21:02.380
we brought you your beloved sukiyaki!

00:21:04.380 --> 00:21:07.380
Mai-san said she had
stopped being a teacher.

00:21:08.630 --> 00:21:11.270
She said, “sorry for lying”.

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:20.550
Rentarou?

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:23.050
Rentarou?

00:21:23.980 --> 00:21:26.280
The meat will go bad.

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:30.730
The night came soon,
as well as the morning…

00:21:30.730 --> 00:21:32.330
And then the night came again.

00:21:43.430 --> 00:21:44.290
That time…

00:21:48.630 --> 00:21:50.380
Shall we kiss?

00:21:52.430 --> 00:21:54.730
We had never kissed before.

00:21:55.680 --> 00:21:58.680
We were no longer the us from back then.

00:21:58.680 --> 00:22:01.860
I had a hunch that my kiss, which tasted like tobacco,

00:22:01.860 --> 00:22:04.080
would have been inexcusable back then.

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:05.480
Ah!

00:22:06.580 --> 00:22:07.300
SHUT UP!

00:22:10.330 --> 00:22:12.880
As well, it seems there will be beautiful weather in Tokyo today.

00:22:15.080 --> 00:22:17.980
Luckily today, we are three as well.

00:22:20.110 --> 00:22:25.800
We are here.

00:22:20.110 --> 00:22:25.630
bokura wa koko ni iru

00:22:26.130 --> 00:22:33.200
We will be here.

00:22:26.130 --> 00:22:33.200
bokura ga koko ni aru

00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:38.520
The slow time is

00:22:33.540 --> 00:22:38.520
yuruyaka na jikan ga

00:22:38.750 --> 00:22:45.450
flowing in this room.

00:22:38.750 --> 00:22:45.450
nagareteru kono heya de

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:49.050
Even if the summer days vanish,

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:49.050
natsu no hi ga kiete mo

00:22:49.280 --> 00:22:53.110
the smiles that remain

00:22:49.280 --> 00:22:53.110
nokoru egao tachi

00:22:53.230 --> 00:22:59.990
are a chain of happiness up to this point.

00:22:53.230 --> 00:22:59.990
kocchi made shiawase no rensa

00:23:00.230 --> 00:23:05.830
Ah, the meaning of honesty,

00:23:00.230 --> 00:23:05.830
aa sunaosa no imi

00:23:06.110 --> 00:23:14.170
is within the innermost depths of your heart.

00:23:06.110 --> 00:23:14.170
KOKORO no zutto zutto oku no hou e

00:23:14.370 --> 00:23:19.550
Hey, the days are wonderful

00:23:14.370 --> 00:23:19.550
nee subarashii hibi

00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:27.310
in the midst of weakness and anxiety.

00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:27.310
yowasa to fuan no naka de shitte

00:23:27.350 --> 00:23:33.860
I won’t say goodbye, Because forever

00:23:27.350 --> 00:23:33.860
sayonara wa iwanai yo datte itsumademo

00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:39.140
the days will be unchanged.

00:23:34.020 --> 00:23:39.140
kawaru koto no nai hibi

00:23:39.270 --> 00:23:45.980
Surely forever. M

00:23:39.270 --> 00:23:45.980
kitto itsumademo

